$${A^2} = \left[ {\matrix{
1 & 2 \cr
{ - 2} & { - 5} \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
1 & 2 \cr
{ - 2} & { - 5} \cr

} } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
{ - 3} & { - 8} \cr
8 & {21} \cr

} } \right]$$

$$\alpha {A^2} + \beta A = \left[ {\matrix{
{ - 3\alpha } & { - 8\alpha } \cr
{8\alpha } & {21\alpha } \cr

} } \right] + \left[ {\matrix{
\beta & {2\beta } \cr
{ - 2\beta } & { - 5\beta } \cr

} } \right]$$

$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
{ - 3\alpha + \beta } & { - 8\alpha + 2\beta } \cr
{8\alpha - 2\beta } & {21\alpha - 5\beta } \cr

} } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
2 & 0 \cr
0 & 2 \cr

} } \right]$$

On Comparing

$$8\alpha = 2\beta ,\, - 3\alpha + \beta = 2,\,21\alpha - 5\beta = 2$$

$$ \Rightarrow \alpha = 2,\,\beta = 8$$

So, $$\alpha + \beta = 10$$
